    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d62">

                <pb facs="0114" n="81" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v23/pg81"/>

                <head>62. Telegram From [<hi rendition="#italic">location not declassified</hi>] to
                    the Central Intelligence Agency<anchor n="1" xml:id="d62-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<hi rendition="#italic">location not
                            declassified</hi>], <date calendar="gregorian" when="1961-01-19">January
                            19, 1961</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>0283 [<hi rendition="#italic">less than 1 line not declassified</hi>]. 1. Thanks
                    for Patrice. If we had known he was coming we would have baked a snake.</p>
                <p>2. Per [<hi rendition="#italic">name not declassified</hi>] GOK had no advance word whatsoever. Lumumba severely beaten at airport by
                    gendarmerie, then taken Jadotville prison where guarded by all white guards.
                        GOK does not plan liquidate Lumumba. [<hi rendition="#italic">name not
                        declassified</hi>] fears chances of Balubakat uprising in Eville
                    considerably increased.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d62-f2"/></p>
                <p>End of message.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d62-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d62-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Central Intelligence Agency Files, [<hi rendition="#italic">text not
                        declassified</hi>], Folder 3. Secret; Routine. Repeated priority to
                    Leopoldville. Received at 0135Z.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d62-f2" n="2" xml:id="d62-f2-content">
                <p>Most of this cable is quoted in <hi rendition="#italic">Interim Report,</hi> p.
                    51.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
